  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Digitoxigenin may interact with Tankyrase-2 through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, Digitoxigenin is shown to have a target relationship with SK-HEP1, which in turn is a target of both Massarinin B and Tankyrase-2. Additionally, Digitoxigenin is linked to SK-HEP1, which is a target of (2S,3R,5R)-2-[(R)-bromo-[(2R,3R,5S,6R)-3,5-dibromo-6-ethyloxan-2-yl]methyl]-5-[(1R)-1-bromoprop-2-ynyl]oxolan-3-ol, which is also a target of Tankyrase-2. The scores for these relationships indicate a moderate level of confidence in the interaction between Digitoxigenin and Tankyrase-2, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The evidence suggests that Digitoxigenin may act through a downstream pathway involving SK-HEP1 and Tankyrase-2, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
